The functions of the entry's record start a fiber in which a writer of a cell runs, and the runtime runs them on the fiber that calls into it, inside a mask: update directly, through a helper, a helper of another module, a method call and a `where` method, view through a helper of a hole, and init at the mount; each writer writes a copy of the contents, so none hosts, accepted (ownership-v3-kernel.md §13 item 12, *A defect*, (d), *The ways in, from the code*, item 12; #2695). Its live twin is CellEntryHostsLive.
